iven-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Eccles</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cough in motor neuron disease: a review of mechanisms</article-title><source>QJM</source><year>1999</year><volume>92</volume><fpage>487</fpage><lpage>494</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10627867</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B25"><label>25</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McCool</surname><given-names>FD</given-names></name><name><surname>Leith</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pathophysiology of cough</article-title><source>Clin Chest Med</source><year>1987</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>189</fpage><lpage>195</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3621873</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B26"><label>26</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmidt-Nowara</surname><given-names>WW</given-names></name><name><surname>Altman</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Atelectasis and neuromuscular respiratory failure</article-title><source>Chest</source><year>1984</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>792</fpage><lpage>795</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6723392</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B27"><label>27</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Estenne</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>De Troyer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The effects of tetraplegia on chest wall statics</article-title><source>Am Rev Respir Dis</source><year>1986</year><volume>134</volume><fpage>121</fpage><lpage>124</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2942066</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Fig. 1</label><caption><p>Relationships between maximal respiratory pressures and UPCF. Both absolute value of MIP and MEP correlated significantly with UPCF. UPCF, Unassisted peak cough flow; MIP, Maximal inspiratory pressure; MEP, Maximal expiratory pressure.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-184-g001"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Fig. 2</label><caption><p>Relationships between maximal respiratory pressures and VPCF. Both absolute value of MIP and MEP correlated significantly with VPCF. VPCF, Volume assisted peak cough flow; MIP, Maximal inspiratory pressure; MEP, Maximal expiratory pressure.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-184-g002"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Fig. 3</label><caption><p>Relationships between maximal respiratory pressures and MPCF. Both absolute value of MIP and MEP correlated significantly with MPCF. MPCF, Manual assisted peak cough flow; MIP, Maximal inspiratory pressure; MEP, Maximal expiratory pressure.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-184-g003"/></fig><fig id="F4" position="float"><label>Fig. 4</label><caption><p>Relationships between maximal respiratory pressures and CPCF. Both absolute value of MIP and MEP correlated significantly with CPCF. CPCF, Combined peak cough flow; MIP, Maximal inspiratory pressure; MEP, Maximal expiratory pressure.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-184-g004"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Comparisons between UPCF<sup>*</sup> and Each Assisted PCF<sup>&#x02020;</sup> (n = 32)</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="ymj-47-184-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Mean values &#x000b1; SD (liters/min).</p><p><sup>*</sup>UPCF = unassisted peak cough flow; <sup>&#x02020;</sup>PCF = peak cough flow; <sup>&#x02021;</sup>VPCF = volume assisted peak cough flow; <sup>&#x000a7;</sup>MPCF = manual assisted peak cough flow; <sup>&#x02225;</sup>CPCF = combined peak cough flow, <sup>&#x000b6;</sup><italic>p</italic> &#x0003c; 0.001, <sup>**</sup>Both the values of VPCF and MPCF, which were similar, were higher than that of UPCF but lower than that of CPCF.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>